      "line": 4,
      "path": "SqliteVerifier.lean",
      "rule": "R13",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The production root module now imports `SqliteVerifier.Examples`, the demonstrations and `SqliteVerifier.ApplicationKeyDemonstration`, but `lakefile.toml:16` still says \"the production root excludes them\". Fix: remove the example imports from the production root, or update the lakefile comment and the library split so that they agree."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261009T093128Z-9c1e4b79#3",
      "line": 49,
      "path": "tools/PublicDocInventory.lean",
      "rule": "R1",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The location of the model package is the literal `\"packages/belay-sqlite\"` inside the source lookup. Fix: define a named, documented constant for the model package directory and use it in the lookup."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261009T093128Z-9c1e4b79#4",
      "line": 62,
      "path": "tools/api_reference.py",
      "rule": "R1",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The model package path `\"packages/belay-sqlite\"` is repeated as a literal (lines 62 and 67), and the namespace `\"Belay\"` is added to an inline set literal in `our_pages` (line 81). Fix: define documented module-level constants for the model package directory and for our public page roots, and use them in these functions."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261009T093128Z-9c1e4b79#5",
      "line": 30,
      "path": "migration_check/import_path.py",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "No test checks that `package_view` adds artifact files for explicitly requested modules, or that `compatible_links` refuses links with different origins in a case-insensitive workspace. The `prepare.py` and `source_closure.py` callers depend on these. Fix: add deterministic tests for a requested module's companion artifacts and for the `compatible_links` refusal and deduplication cases."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261009T093128Z-9c1e4b79#6",
      "line": 92,
      "path": "migration_check/import_path.py",
      "rule": "R10",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The message \"Module paths must be relative names within the supplied roots\" does not name the path that failed or say what the user can do next. Fix: include the bad module path in the message and tell the user to give a relative Lean module path with no `.` or `..` parts."
    }
